Treating each listed pair as one undirected edge, the total number of 3-stars is

\[
\sum_{v} \binom{d_v}{3}
\]

where \(d_v\) is the degree of node \(v\).

The degree-count distribution from the graph is:

\[
\begin{aligned}
&6:3,\ 7:2,\ 8:4,\ 9:8,\ 10:6,\ 11:5,\ 12:5,\ 13:5,\ 14:8,\ 15:5,\\
&16:3,\ 17:3,\ 18:2,\ 19:3,\ 20:2,\ 21:3,\ 22:4,\ 23:4,\ 24:1,\ 36:1.
\end{aligned}
\]

So,

\[
\begin{aligned}
\sum_v \binom{d_v}{3}
&=3\binom{6}{3}+2\binom{7}{3}+4\binom{8}{3}+8\binom{9}{3}
+\cdots+\binom{24}{3}+\binom{36}{3}\\
&=47225.
\end{aligned}
\]

